brothels a hurry fled the war in Syria  four years ago after her home in Homs  was bombed she and her family now live  in this Lebanese refugee camp when she  first got to Lebanon what worked packing  boxes earning just four dollars a day  then an NGO called beyond rescued her  from that job and got her into a school  near the camp today the 16 year old is  about to head out to her poetry class  after years of trauma and uncertainty  Bob is beginning to find her voice and  she's learning to write verse for the  first time in her life knowledge Elia  the generation whose life is lost his  dreams have been broken by war we are  the generation that has grown too old  too soon this poem recounts the  challenges Bob faces as a refugee kate  famiiy has we're always attacking us  with words the Lebanese always ask who  are you where did you come from why did  you come here a two hours drive from the  camp the UN Children's Organization  UNICEF has organized an exhibition about  art and refugees at Beirut's civil war  memorial  this painting is inspired by the words  of our thoughts and feelings of dozens  of Syrian children and on display in  this exhibition in Beirut moved by the  poems and letters Syrian and Lebanese  artists have come together and are using  their creativity to describe the  experiences of these children of war  avant depths is one of the artists he's  tried to capture wild sentiments on  canvas this is not sadness this is this  is anger and and I I didn't want to show  the children as victims  the organizers deliberately chose the  memorial as the site for the event  Lebanon itself suffered through decades  of civil war there's nearly tore the  country apart  [Music]  civilians have been the main victims of  the conflict in Syria which has  especially targeted the country's young  many of the children that have written  these poems and texts have lived the war  very intensively they have lost their  homes their school sometimes their  parents back at the camp  fathers Ahuja is on her way to a  get-together with some friends she's now  taken up singing as well and says she'd  like to be a journalist or a singer when  she grows up  Walt has lost nearly everything but she  refuses to give up hope  [Music]
 

